{"availability":"available","full":"10apashmeenkaur-boop/Nodeflow","name":"Nodeflow","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-09T21:49:34Z","updated":"2026-10-09T22:17:24Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://nodeflow-chi.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://nodeflow-chi.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:04.182Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:04.182Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:04.182Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:04.182Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A visual workflow builder with hand-written SVG wiring, typed connection rules, and full undo/redo.","Drag nodes onto a grid, wire outputs to inputs, and build automation flows like \"when someone signs up → check if they're verified → send a welcome email\". Every change can be undone, every connection is validated, and the whole workflow exports to (and renders from) clean JSON."],"features":["Drag nodes from a searchable library (or click to add, or right-click → Add node here). There are 9 node types: Webhook, Schedule, Condition, Delay, Code, Send Email, HTTP Request, Slack Message and Log.","Wire outputs to inputs from either end. Within 16px of a valid port the wire snaps on, invalid ports fade out, and dropping on a taken input rewires it.","Add extra ports with + (shown in italics) and remove them on hover. Built-in ports can't be removed because they define the node.","Rename nodes (double-click, right-click or the Inspector), delete with Del, and use right-click menus everywhere.","Tidy up (Shift+Alt+F): automatic left-to-right layout by graph depth that minimises wire crossings and never routes a wire under a node. Nodes glide to their new places."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/10apashmeenkaur-boop/Nodeflow/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"eb4da866aa883bc61ebe56d4158110ebd4259